    "https://www.longwood.edu/career/career-success-for-longwood-students/": {
      "title": "Career Success for Longwood Students",
      "description": "Career Success for Longwood Students - Longwood University There are active notices and/or alerts. Visit the Alerts site for details >> Academics Admissions Lancer Life About Us Visit Apply Give Lancer Dashboard Lancer Dashboard Today is Saturday, September 05, 2026 Services myLongwood Live Mail Canvas DegreeWorks Advising Lancer Web Card Center Student Housing Gateway (RMS) Lancer Link (Clubs & Orgs) Box Tk20 OTP Applications Watermark - Students Handshake Change My Password Dining Dining Locations, Hours & Menus Change Meal Plan Dining Services Website Information Help Desk LancerCard Career Success Greenwood Library Recreation / Fitness Center Bookstore Academic Departments & Programs All Offices & Services Resources Course Search Student Handbook Farmville Area Bus (FAB) Academic Calendar Exam Schedule How Do I... ? Suggestions/Complaints More Academic Resources Career Success for Longwood Students Home Academics Academic Offices & Resources Career Success Career Success for Longwood Students Your future starts here. At Longwood, career success is part of your journey from day one. Through the Civitae Core Curriculum, hands-on internships, and personal coaching, you’ll build the skills and confidence to thrive in any career path. The Center for Career Success is here to support you every step of the way — from choosing a major to landing your first job or graduate school acceptance. Career Coaching & Appointments Book a Coaching Session Meet one-on-one with a Career Coach (in-person or virtual) for resume help, interview prep, exploring majors, or graduate school planning. Career Fairs and Networking Events See Upcoming Career Events Meet employers, grad schools, and alumni at Longwood’s career fairs and workshops. Build confidence, explore opportunities, and grow your network. Internships Find Your Internship Apply classroom learning in real workplaces. Over 80% of Lancers complete internships, gaining experience, building skills, and earning credit toward graduation. Work Shadow Program Apply for Work Shadow Spend a day with an alum or professional to explore careers, observe daily work, and get advice that helps you plan your future. Micro-Internships Apply for a Micro-Internship Short-term projects (about 20 hours) that build skills, expand your resume, and connect you with employers. Earn a $500 stipend while exploring career paths. Mentorship Program Tap into Your Network Build connections at Longwood through mentorship. Explore opportunities to meet professionals, gain advice, and grow your network. Career Closet Choose free, professional attire for interviews, internships, and career fairs — giving you the confidence to make a strong first impression. Find out more Handshake: Your Career Hub Handshake is your go-to platform for jobs, internships, and career events. With over one million employers nationwide, it’s the easiest way to connect with opportunities that match your interests. Through Longwood’s Handshake page, you can: Search and apply for jobs and internships Register for career fairs, workshops, and events Access career resources tailored to your goals Schedule appointments with Career Coaches Get Started: Log in to Handshake using your Longwood credentials at longwood.joinhandshake.com . Build your profile, upload your resume, and start exploring opportunities today. Important: For first-time users, you will need to complete a brief activation process, which takes 5 minutes or less. This process includes answering a few questions to help customize the platform’s content for you. Once your account is activated, you will have access to Handshake as long as you are enrolled at Longwood or are an alumnus with an active Longwood email address. About Us Admissions Academics Lancer Life Academic Calendar Bookstore Careers at Longwood Library A-Z Index Offices & Services Solomon (Faculty & Staff) Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909 (434) 395-2000 Maps & Directions Privacy Statement FOIA Student Consumer Information Non-Discrimination Statement Freedom of Expression Policies Alerts & Notices Longwood University Accessibility Statement © All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.longwood.edu/career/career-success-services-for-longwood-alumni/": {
      "title": "Career Success Services for Longwood Alumni",
      "description": "Career Success Services for Longwood Alumni - Longwood University There are active notices and/or alerts. Visit the Alerts site for details >> Academics Admissions Lancer Life About Us Visit Apply Give Lancer Dashboard Lancer Dashboard Today is Saturday, September 05, 2026 Services myLongwood Live Mail Canvas DegreeWorks Advising Lancer Web Card Center Student Housing Gateway (RMS) Lancer Link (Clubs & Orgs) Box Tk20 OTP Applications Watermark - Students Handshake Change My Password Dining Dining Locations, Hours & Menus Change Meal Plan Dining Services Website Information Help Desk LancerCard Career Success Greenwood Library Recreation / Fitness Center Bookstore Academic Departments & Programs All Offices & Services Resources Course Search Student Handbook Farmville Area Bus (FAB) Academic Calendar Exam Schedule How Do I... ? Suggestions/Complaints More Academic Resources Career Success Services for Longwood Alumni Home Academics Academic Offices & Resources Career Success Career Success Services for Longwood Alumni Career Support and Connection for Longwood Alumni No matter where your career takes you, Longwood University is here to support your professional growth. From career coaching and resume reviews to volunteer opportunities and mentorship, our alumni services help you advance your goals while staying connected to the Lancer community. Career Coaching Book an Appointment Whether you graduated last year or decades ago, our career coaches offer personalized guidance to help you navigate career changes, prepare for new opportunities, or update your professional materials. Services include: Career exploration sessions Resume and cover letter reviews Online profile development (LinkedIn, Handshake) Job and internship search support Interview preparation Graduate school application guidance Volunteer Opportunities Learn More About Volunteering Share your experience and expertise with current students by serving as a mentor, networking professional, or event speaker. Volunteer roles include: Career Ambassador at fairs and networking events Professional Interview participant Panelist or guest speaker Work Shadow host Micro-internship host Mentorship Program Become a Mentor Build a meaningful, semester-long connection with a student whose career interests align with your own. Mentors meet with their mentee at least three times, providing insights, guidance, and professional perspective. Stay Connected Get Started with Handshake Alumni can access Handshake for job postings, networking, and event registration. Email career@longwood.edu with your name, graduation year, and major to get started. About Us Admissions Academics Lancer Life Academic Calendar Bookstore Careers at Longwood Library A-Z Index Offices & Services Solomon (Faculty & Staff) Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909 (434) 395-2000 Maps & Directions Privacy Statement FOIA Student Consumer Information Non-Discrimination Statement Freedom of Expression Policies Alerts & Notices Longwood University Accessibility Statement © All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.longwood.edu/career/career-success-services-for-employers/": {
      "title": "Career Success Services for Employers",
      "description": "Career Success Services for Employers - Longwood University There are active notices and/or alerts. Visit the Alerts site for details >> Academics Admissions Lancer Life About Us Visit Apply Give Lancer Dashboard Lancer Dashboard Today is Saturday, September 05, 2026 Services myLongwood Live Mail Canvas DegreeWorks Advising Lancer Web Card Center Student Housing Gateway (RMS) Lancer Link (Clubs & Orgs) Box Tk20 OTP Applications Watermark - Students Handshake Change My Password Dining Dining Locations, Hours & Menus Change Meal Plan Dining Services Website Information Help Desk LancerCard Career Success Greenwood Library Recreation / Fitness Center Bookstore Academic Departments & Programs All Offices & Services Resources Course Search Student Handbook Farmville Area Bus (FAB) Academic Calendar Exam Schedule How Do I... ? Suggestions/Complaints More Academic Resources Career Success Services for Employers Home Academics Academic Offices & Resources Career Success Career Success Services for Employers Partner with Longwood: Connect with Tomorrow’s Leaders At Longwood University, we prepare students to be adaptable, thoughtful, and ready to contribute from day one. More than 80% of Lancers complete an internship before graduation, gaining real-world experience that gives them a competitive edge. Through our Civitae Core Curriculum —Longwood’s signature pathway to citizen leadership—students intentionally build the critical thinking, communication, and problem-solving skills that matter most in today’s workplace. When you hire a Lancer, you gain a collaborative, curious, and community-minded emerging professional who is ready to grow with your organization and make a meaningful impact. Career Fairs Learn more about Career Fairs Meet talented students face-to-face at our annual recruiting events, including our University-Wide Career, Internship, and Graduate School Fair and our Teacher Recruitment Day. Micro-Internships Learn more about Micro-Internships Host a short-term, high-impact project to engage students while gaining fresh perspectives for your organization. Work Shadow Program Learn more about Work Shadow Give students a behind-the-scenes look at your workplace and industry through one-day or multi-day shadowing experiences. Get Started with Handshake Handshake is Longwood University’s career management platform, connecting employers with students and alumni for jobs, internships, and career events. With over one million employers already on the platform, Handshake makes it simple to post opportunities, connect with qualified candidates, and register for career fairs or networking events. To get started, visit Longwood’s Handshake page and create an employer account. Once approved, you can: Post jobs and internships directly to Longwood students and alumni Search student profiles and resumes Register for upcoming career events Post Jobs and Internships Reach Longwood students and alumni directly by posting positions through Handshake, our career services platform. Post a Job or Internship If you need assistance getting started, refer to this step-by-step guide: How to Post a Job on Handshake About Us Admissions Academics Lancer Life Academic Calendar Bookstore Careers at Longwood Library A-Z Index Offices & Services Solomon (Faculty & Staff) Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909 (434) 395-2000 Maps & Directions Privacy Statement FOIA Student Consumer Information Non-Discrimination Statement Freedom of Expression Policies Alerts & Notices Longwood University Accessibility Statement © All rights reserved."
    },
